msgid "Click **start building**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:89
msgid "Choose the **Classic** mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:97
msgid "**2.2 If This - the trigger**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:99
msgid "Click **Add** next to **If This**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:105
msgid "Search for **webhook** and click **Webhooks**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:111
msgid "Click **Receive a web request**. This is the service the board will call."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:117
msgid "Set the **Event Name** to **vibration_detected**, then click **Create trigger**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:121
msgid "This name becomes part of the address, so it has to match the ``URL`` in the sketch. If you use another name here, change it there too."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:130
msgid "**2.3 Then That - the action**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:132
msgid "Click **Add** next to **Then That** to add an action."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:138
msgid "Search for **email** and click **Email**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:144
msgid "Click **Send me an email**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:150
msgid "Write the subject and the body of the email."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:152
msgid "For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:154
msgid "**Subject**: ``Detected vibration!!!``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:155
msgid "**Body**: ``Detected vibration, please confirm the situation promptly! {{OccurredAt}}``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:157
msgid "``{{OccurredAt}}`` is replaced by IFTTT with the exact time the event happened, which is handy when you look at the mail the next morning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:164
msgid "Finish the wizard by following the screens below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:175
msgid "3. Run the Code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:177
msgid "Open the ``04-Vibration_alert_system.ino`` file under the path of ``ultimate-sensor-kit\\code\\iot_project_espc201\\wifi\\04-Vibration_alert_system``, or copy this code into **Arduino IDE**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:180
msgid "Type the name and password of your own Wi-Fi network."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:187
msgid "Open the **My Applets** page of IFTTT and click the applet you just created."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:192
msgid "Copy your webhook URL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:199
msgid "Paste the whole address IFTTT shows you into ``URL`` - **https:// and all**, exactly as you copied it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:206
msgid "You do not have to cut anything off. The sketch keeps only the part after the host name before it sends the request, because the module talks plain TCP to port 80."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:211
msgid "Select **Arduino UNO R4 Minima** and the right port, then click **Upload**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:213
msgid "Open the Serial Monitor at **115200**. After a few seconds you should read:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:222
msgid "If it says ``FAILED (check ssid and password)``, the board cannot join your network - check the Wi-Fi name and password, and remember that the ESPC2-01 only works on **2.4 GHz** networks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:230
msgid "Tap the sensor. The monitor answers with"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:240
msgid "and an email arrives within a few seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:244
msgid "Knock it twice in a row: the second time only prints ``An alert was sent recently, so this one is skipped.`` That is the two-minute rule at work, not a fault."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:249
msgid "4. Code explanation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:251
msgid "**The serial port that talks to the module**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:253
msgid "The ESPC2-01 is not running this sketch - it works as a modem. The board sends it AT commands on D0/D1, which is ``Serial1``, a hardware port, so 115200 works without bit errors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:261
msgid "**What you have to fill in**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:272
msgid "You copy the address the way IFTTT shows it, **https:// and all**, and the sketch converts it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:285
msgid "``myHOST`` and ``myPORT`` never change: IFTTT always answers on port 80 of ``maker.ifttt.com``. Only the path is personal, because it carries your key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:290
msgid "Why not send ``https://`` straight to the module? HTTPS means TLS: the module would have to open a secure connection with certificates, which is a much longer AT sequence. IFTTT accepts the same request on plain **port 80**, so the short way is enough here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:294
msgid "**Vibration pin and the two-minute rule**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:303
msgid "The SW-420 gives a simple level: it goes **HIGH while it shakes**. Without the two-minute rule a single knock would fire dozens of emails."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:306
msgid "**espModuleInit() - wake the module up first**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:308
msgid "The module needs about a second to boot and prints its start-up log on the same wire. This function waits for the word ``ready`` and then sends ``ATE0`` so the replies stop carrying a copy of the command you just sent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:330
msgid "The ``buf.length() < 512`` guard matters: without it a module that keeps talking would keep the inner loop busy for ever and the sketch would never reach ``setup()``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:333
msgid "**at() - one AT command, with a time limit**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:352
msgid "Every command goes through this one function: it sends, collects the reply, and stops as soon as the expected answer - or an error - shows up. It **always returns**, so the board can never freeze on a missing ``OK``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:356
msgid "**setup() and loop()**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:377
msgid "If the Wi-Fi is down at start-up, the sketch does not give up: it tries again every 30 seconds. That is why you can start the board before the router is ready."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:380
msgid "**sendAlert() - one HTTP request**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:396
msgid "Three AT commands do the job:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:398
msgid "``AT+CIPMUX=0`` - one connection at a time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:399
msgid "``AT+CIPSTART`` - open a TCP connection to ``maker.ifttt.com:80``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:400
msgid "``AT+CIPSEND=<length>`` - the module answers with ``>``, and only then you send the text of the request. The length must be the exact number of characters, which is why the sketch measures ``req.length()`` instead of guessing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:404
msgid "The request itself is the same thing your browser sends: a line with the method and the path, one header, an empty line, and nothing else. IFTTT fires the applet as soon as it reads the path."
msgstr ""
